Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software depends on, but does not bundle, the following components. Each
is governed by its own license; this NOTICE does not relicense them.

- github.com/matthupy/videosift (MIT) — video frame extraction. Execs the
  external ffmpeg and ffprobe binaries at runtime.
- github.com/spf13/cobra, github.com/spf13/viper (Apache-2.0) — CLI + config.
- github.com/prometheus/client_golang (Apache-2.0) — metrics.
- golang.org/x/sync (BSD-3-Clause) — errgroup.
- github.com/hibiken/asynq (MIT) — Redis-backed queue (M5; not yet wired).

The Azure AI Content Safety adapter calls Microsoft's hosted REST API and is
subject to Microsoft's terms. Per Microsoft policy, Azure AI Content Safety
MUST NOT be used to detect child sexual abuse material (CSAM); CSAM is handled
by the hash-match seam (not the classifier) — see RESPONSIBLE_USE.md.

ffmpeg and ffprobe are NOT distributed with this source. The Docker runtime
stage installs them from the base image's package repository under their own
licenses (LGPL/GPL depending on build).

PhotoDNA is licensed-access only and is NEVER bundled or redistributed here.
